<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Sx2.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.T5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The results of distance-based and GSP on Modelnet40 and ScanObjectNN dataset with PointClip V2 as VLM backbone.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.22375v1/Rebuttal_Fig2.svg" id="Sx2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/271;" width="548" height="271"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Error rates of pseudo prompts with different filtering ratio <math id="Sx2.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2506.22375v1/Figures/Figure3.png" id="Sx2.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/285;" width="548" height="285" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation Study on the Impact of Negative Prompts: Blue Bars Indicate Results Without Negative Prompts, While Yellow Bars Indicate Results With Negative Prompts. All Experiments Conducted on the ScanObjNN Dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Incorrect pseudo prompts</span>: Self-training is known to be sensitive to incorrect pseudo labels. To further analyze the impact of pseudo prompt selection, we vary <math id="Sx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> from 2 to 20 and examine the error rate on selected pseudo prompts (Fig. <a href="#Sx2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ B. Additional Studies ‣ Exploiting Vision Language Model for Training-Free 3D Point Cloud OOD Detection via Graph Score Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). As <math id="Sx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> decreases (stricter selection), the error rate on pseudo prompts reduces. On average, <math id="Sx2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=5</annotation></semantics></math> proves to be an effective hyperparameter for selecting reliable pseudo prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Study of negative prompt</span>: The ablation study in Fig <a href="#Sx2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ B. Additional Studies ‣ Exploiting Vision Language Model for Training-Free 3D Point Cloud OOD Detection via Graph Score Propagation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> evaluates the impact of negative prompts on ScanObjectNN Dataset, the results reveal a consistent performance gap between models with and without negative prompts.</p>
</div>
